{"id": "EUVD-2026-81921", "enisaUuid": "f9c972f3-6dcc-3bc0-8236-5a9fb3a8044c", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nALSA: control: Don't add invalid kcontrols to LED layer\n\nThe kcontrol LED state layer tries to track the all associated\nkcontrol elements with naive assumptions that they are readable.\nBut one can create a write-only element that has no get callback (even\na user element can do it), and this may lead to a NULL dereference at\nthe call chain of snd_ctl_led_notify(), as found by syzkaller.\n\nFor avoiding the Oops, add a sanity check of the kcontrol's info and\nget callbacks, and just skip the invalid kcontrols before assigning\nthe kctl to the LED layer.", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T16:05:44", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:49:38", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6e152cbfac3a2a62f79df7d23d621917c20367eb", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3b8a540b36aa064822c701e4e0a1dea2cd4ec5b0", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3d20cd049fc5f51f80e24a2db7a3cf00593c79e4", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2f0c97b1a32fba8e81a69f6231aa0b3c9b6bc581", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/18c08f84ca483029f04e426ec7ca3b5d3684cf22", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/74e3b979ce8b78a690f8b94ccf2e2c965f7f5c11"], "aliases": ["GHSA-pxhq-v7w3-j8wf", "CVE-2026-90060"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0eb3f8fa-82ea-314c-80ef-954686b0e52b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.6"}, {"id": "1e78cd9f-4cbb-3087-924a-64a27697f534", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "22d8de62f11b287b279f1d4473a78c7d5e53e7bc <2f0c97b1a32fba8e81a69f6231aa0b3c9b6bc581"}, {"id": "26a3e02e-fb01-3ad9-8605-2c06eaa46573", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "2dde183c-eea9-34ca-b456-c28bd8ef093e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "22d8de62f11b287b279f1d4473a78c7d5e53e7bc <18c08f84ca483029f04e426ec7ca3b5d3684cf22"}, {"id": "380f2281-415c-3678-9076-a2342c79eba9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "22d8de62f11b287b279f1d4473a78c7d5e53e7bc <6e152cbfac3a2a62f79df7d23d621917c20367eb"}, {"id": "4ee91bbf-4a16-3c97-a08f-b6b14a25535e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.110"}, {"id": "64c959ec-5323-3586-9211-35fed4894720", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "66ee9897-5f00-3077-a931-78709bddf698", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.52"}, {"id": "9f51332a-960b-32cb-a4cd-59518126d34a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "22d8de62f11b287b279f1d4473a78c7d5e53e7bc <3b8a540b36aa064822c701e4e0a1dea2cd4ec5b0"}, {"id": "b09457bb-56f5-30b6-909a-ce378b8d7fa9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.13"}, {"id": "b9926f56-2827-37d2-959d-0fb304533310", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "22d8de62f11b287b279f1d4473a78c7d5e53e7bc <74e3b979ce8b78a690f8b94ccf2e2c965f7f5c11"}, {"id": "be4cb37c-d911-3f5e-a3c3-bd5da6beb21d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1.188"}, {"id": "d8321c68-c6ef-366f-9004-52f3f10ae918", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "22d8de62f11b287b279f1d4473a78c7d5e53e7bc <3d20cd049fc5f51f80e24a2db7a3cf00593c79e4"}, {"id": "df0874e8-0b13-3311-adc5-04dbba89dbf6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "e509f69a-c4d4-33b0-bc85-f824c9e97e0c", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}